From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:25:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: compute shaders in software

The compute engine's dispatches run: its program (found and translated as a draw's stages
are, through Eden's compute environment), its constant buffers from the launch description,
textures from the compute engine's pools and storage buffers from the constant buffers. Each
workgroup's invocations run 16 at a time, with shared memory, their local and workgroup ids,
and atomics on shared memory, storage buffers and global memory (32-bit integer ones, and
float adds). A program with barriers runs each group of 16 to the barrier, saving where it
stopped, then the next, until all are past it.
